jective <ACCENT_0003>tale morphism\n<MATH_0011>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nNote that <MATH_0012> is a <MATH_0013>-covering.\nNote that each <MATH_0014> is an <ACCENT_0004>tale covering,\nhence a <MATH_0015>-covering. Hence <MATH_0016> is a\n<MATH_0017>-covering of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0018>. But since <MATH_0019> and each <MATH_0020>\nis a scheme we see that <MATH_0021> is a\n<MATH_0022>-covering of schemes over <MATH_0023>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nNow we have\n<MATHSEG_0001> has <MATHSEG_0002> has <MATHSEG_0003>each <MATHSEG_0004> has <MATHSEG_0005>each <MATHSEG_0006> has <MATHSEG_0007>\nthe first and last equivalence by the definition of\n<MATH_0024> the middle equivalence because we assumed\n<MATH_0025> is local on the source in the <MATH_0026>-topology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bacb2de2055e015389d4b090a439b3443a86e51e345138f7e30e55260468b872", "unit_id": "tag:06ER:proof"}
